This can be done by direct computation: It turns out that $p - \theta \circ \partial _ z$ evaluated on $z^ i\xi ^{[n]}$ gives zero except for $1$ which is mapped to $p$ and $\xi $ which is mapped to $-p\lambda $. It turns out that $(\theta \otimes 1) \circ \text{d}_1 - \text{d}_1 \circ \theta $ evaluated on $z^ i\xi ^{[n]}$ gives zero except for $z^{p - 1}\xi $ which is mapped to $-\lambda $.